[00:00.48]Lesson 14 | 第14课
[00:02.45]A noble gangster | 高贵的歹徒
[00:09.81]How did Hawkwood make money in times of peace? | 霍克伍德在和平时期是怎样赚钱的？
[00:15.20]There was a time when the owners of shops and businesses in Chicago had to pay large sums of money to gangsters in return for 'protection'. | 曾经有一个时期，芝加哥的店主和企业主不得不把大笔的钱交给歹徒，以换取“保护”。
[00:26.33]If the money was not paid promptly, the gangsters would quickly put a man out of business by destroying his shop. | 如果钱交得不及时，歹徒就会捣毁他的商店，很快让他做不成生意。
[00:35.46]Obtaining 'protection money' is not a modern crime. | 勒索“保护费”并不是一种现代的罪恶行径。
[00:39.67]As long ago as the fourteenth century, an Englishman, Sir John Hawkwood, made the remarkable discovery that people would rather pay large sums of money than have their life work destroyed by gangsters. | 早在14世纪，英国人约翰·霍克伍德爵士就有一项惊人的发现：人们宁愿掏大笔的钱，也不愿让自己的毕生心血被歹徒毁掉。
[00:56.51]Six hundred years ago, Sir John Hawkwood arrived in Italy with a band of soldiers and settled near Florence. | 600年前，约翰·霍克伍德爵士带着一队士兵来到意大利，定居在佛罗伦萨附近。
[01:05.36]He soon made a name for himself and came to be known to the Italians as Giovanni Acuto. | 他很快就出了名，意大利人叫他乔瓦尼·阿库托。
[01:13.45]Whenever the Italian city-states were at war with each other, Hawkwood used to hire his soldiers to princes who were willing to pay the high price he demanded. | 每当意大利的城邦之间交战时，霍克伍德就把他的士兵雇佣给愿意付出他索要的高价的君主们。
[01:25.40]In times of peace, when business was bad, Hawkwood and his men would march into a city-state, and after burning down a few farms, would offer to go away if protection money was paid to them. | 在和平时期、生意清淡时，霍克伍德和他的士兵就会开进某个城邦，烧掉几座农庄之后主动提出，只要付给他们保护费，他们便撤离。
[01:40.29]Hawkwood made large sums of money in this way. | 霍克伍德用这种手段赚了大笔的钱。
[01:44.35]In spite of this, the Italians regarded him as a sort of hero. | 尽管如此，意大利人还是把他视为某种英雄。
[01:49.86]When he died at the age of eighty, the Florentines gave him a state funeral and had a picture painted which was dedicated to the memory of 'the most valiant soldier and most notable leader, Signor Giovanni Haukodue'. | 他80岁去世时，佛罗伦萨人为他举行了国葬，并作画一幅，以纪念“最勇敢的战士、最杰出的领袖乔瓦尼·霍克伍德阁下”。
